mantle rm430
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_disa_millley
title the hood with two brims
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk turns_an_oilcloth_hood_to_share_its_dry_side
likes hard_cheese stars fresh_straw first_warm_day
dislikes smoke deep_mud
fears a_wet_letter_with_an_unreadable_name
hopes to_keep_a_dry_corner_for_family
topics home +0.4 friends +0.3 weather +0.3 work +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=close refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# turns an oilcloth brim to shelter a second muzzle and listens carefully to what a traveller says under cover.

words
oath! = Oil my second brim | By the dry seam
saying! = A spare corner earns its oil | Walk close and the hood goes further
hood = my doubled brim | the stiff oiled edge
fold = my second fold | a spare oilcloth corner
pin = a flat-headed pin | the short hood pin
straw = a clean straw braid | a twist of fresh straw
cheese = a sharp dry wedge | a thumb of cheese
star = a pinprick above the brim | a faint cold star
wind = the draught at ear height | the wind under a hood
pocket = my inner pocket | the oilcloth flap
paper = a folded order | a clean scrap
shine = an oily gleam | a slate-coloured shine
muck = the thick street mud | a layer of black mire
oil = a drop of linseed oil | the oil on my thumb

any
opinion dole for 3 : I've tasted the use of a public pot. My hand went in shaking and came out steady enough to carry supper.
opinion strangers for 2 : A visitor under my hood can tell me which goods last the journey after I have seen the payment.
opinion watch against 1 : A nose inserted under an oilcloth without leave is still an impertinence when it comes with a badge.
opinion times against 1 : I've learnt which direction a dole queue moves from a closer view than I expected.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : If a trader keeps your paper and the parcel dry, that's some small part of the price returned already.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come on the dry-brim side. | I can make a corner free for a new muzzle.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome as far as the good seam. | Say it across the parcel.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. My hood's still got its shape. | Early enough to try the light side.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening comes beneath both brims. | Draw a little nearer the light.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family fit inside the widest fold. | A dry corner with the family claim on it.
line again.open : Another walk under the same brim. | Your face appears on this side again.
line greet.return : Here. I'd know a greeting through oilcloth. | Welcome to the covered bit.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I've kept the good fold towards you. | Your voice fits here pleasantly.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Speak while I pin the loose end. | I'll listen across this small bit of business.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. A little light still under the brim. | Glad of a voice at this quieter hour.
line farewell : Dry ears to the next doorway. | Mind the paper under your coat.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the fold turned in your favour. | May the rain fall behind your shoulders.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Good lamplight and a snug collar. | A dry way past the late turnings.
line react.news : What's travelled safely under the wrapping? | Let me hear the dry part.
line react.news.new : New word beneath my cover. | That arrived with its fold unbroken.
line react.news.known : I've seen under that flap already. | I know what came through in that parcel.
line react.news.doubt : I'd check that the ink hasn't run two words together. | One wet corner can change a very tidy account.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A hood has enough room for quiet sorrow. | Walk easy. I'll come on the windward side.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Warm news makes a good lining. | That's a little star in a dull fold.
line ask.how : What's been getting inside your collar? | Had any shelter in your day?
line answer.how : Steady beneath my proper fold. | I can turn a stiff breeze out without complaint.
line decline : I'd sooner keep this dry interval for the family. | I need my free hand for a parcel just now.
line accept_decline : You know best where your dry ground lies. | Very well. I won't lean on the matter.
line thank : I'll remember that welcome corner. | You've saved me a folded worry.
line sympathise : Here, let the brim catch some of it. | My shoulder can keep that wind off you.
line reassure : A wet page can dry if it's opened gently. | I'll wait here while you smooth the corners.
line preclose : I've a loose fold needing a pin. | I'd best get this parcel into shelter.

scene fold
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made #hood# broad enough for an unexpected guest.
b : Two wolves under that? | Doesn't the rain collect there?
a : One whole wolf and an additional nose. A surprisingly useful capacity. | It travels down the far edge. Turn the fold before inviting the nose.

scene widestar
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch the stars between the two folds of my hood.
b : Can't you take it off? | How many stars fit inside the gap?
a : Certainly. But the folds keep the street lamps out of my eyes. | Three in the gap if I stand with one shoulder against the wall.

scene cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #cheese# in the pocket the seam protects.
b : Do you always have cheese? | To keep it dry?
a : When I don't I have a satisfactorily shaped space for hope. | My bread disagrees with getting wet. The cheese makes quite a tidy lid.

scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tuck fresh straw above the hem to dry my damp hood lining.
b : Does it itch? | What happens to the straw?
a : It would if I put my head in before taking the bundle out. | I use it for a floor cloth stuffing. A good bit of straw can have several honest careers.

scene sun
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first warm day brings a fine soft gloss out of oilcloth.
b : Do you put it away then? | Does it smell nice?
a : I carry it over my arm. Sunshine has never signed me an all-day guarantee. | A little warm oil and dry straw. Much kinder than a day beside the smoke.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hood can catch smoke as readily as it sheds drops.
b : How do you free the smoke? | Would you change hoods?
a : Shake it inside out, well away from the face. I try not to smoke my own nose twice. | I mend an inconvenience before I go buying a second inconvenience.

scene mud
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In deep mud I pin my oilcloth a little higher.
b : To clear the hem? | What about your ankles?
a : Mud likes a low hem the way a small merchant likes a full shelf. | My ankles can wipe much more cheaply than a length of oilcloth.

scene pair
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd always turn the broad fold towards #self.spouse#.
b : Even on your wet side? | A small kindness?
a : A short way with a wet ear won't do me much harm. | Of course. It's the small ones one can give every time.

scene child
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want #self.child# to know a dry hiding place for a very private paper.
b : What sort of paper? | Where is it?
a : One a child has drawn or folded or chosen. The privacy's the important part. | I'd show it privately, naturally. A family promise ought to have a waterproof seam.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For #self.friend# I'd carry a parcel inside the good fold all the way home.
b : Without opening it? | Wouldn't it make a lump?
a : Rain would be a poor excuse for curiosity. I can keep both out. | One I had agreed to carry. That's a different sort of lump altogether.

scene shop
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I fold a damp order open from the driest corner.
b : What for? | Why not begin at the seal?
a : The names generally survive there. A name with a wet letter missing is an expensive guess. | I'd like the paper to come apart without half the writing moving to the wrong face.

scene hoodtalk
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Travellers give good accounts when their collars are properly sheltered.
b : Which accounts? | Do you ask a lot?
a : Which shop sold a lasting needle. Which stretch of road shook the pins out of poor wrapping. | I seldom need to. A quiet ear and a little privacy are very competent questioners.

scene workshop
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my hood down through part of the Works.
b : For the light? | To listen?
a : For the shadows. They show me what's approaching beyond the bend. | For the clatter that says a cart is coming even when my eyes can't yet see the wheels.

scene cost
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bargain's sound if I know exactly what the dearer bit of it buys.
b : What about show? | What's worth paying for?
a : A little shine can be useful at dusk. I don't universally condemn a bit of polish. | The stitch you can't see because the fold has protected it for several years.

scene loan
when topic=smalltalk self.owes=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An amount outstanding has an unfortunate way of finding all the dry room inside my head.
b : Would you keep a written reckoning? | Can other thoughts still find their way in?
a : Yes. One dry slip to remember what actually has to be paid, and when. | I take it out and look at it once a day. Imagined figures grow faster than proper ones.

scene shelter
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A blessing offered below an eave gives the mouth less work.
b : Why so? | Does the eave bless anybody?
a : A dry muzzle catches the quieter words much more easily. | It keeps the drops off. What the Bright One does with a small practical kindness is private.

scene wish
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed I had a hood big enough for the entire street.
b : Did everyone fit? | Could you walk in it?
a : End to end. The folk at either hem were having an entirely different conversation. | I could just about turn over in bed. The street had to provide its own feet.

scene supper
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set the hood over a chair back while supper's cooking.
b : Why there? | Isn't that somebody's chair?
a : Air goes all through it and the fold keeps its shape. I do like things to earn their drying space. | I can lift a hood with less trouble than finding another good chair for company.

story drip [topic=memories]
  : I once tied my hood off to dry over a low peg. Every drop from its far corner fell into a small cup I hadn't noticed below.
  : On going back to the peg I found nearly a mouthful of water and a pin perfectly clean at the bottom. I'd lost that pin a week before.
  b : Was it in the hood all that time?
  : Under the brim. The water put it back in my hands more neatly than a whole hour's searching.

story starspot [topic=pastimes]
  : I mistook a bright stitch in my oilcloth for a star one night. Turning my muzzle made it travel past two chimney pots with me.
  : I wanted to be sure, so I took the hood off. The stitch dimmed while a surprising number of real stars came clear.
  b : Did you leave the hood off?
  : Briefly. I wore it afterwards with a much better idea what my own light was worth.

story cheeserag [topic=food]
  : I once folded a cheese and a clean sewing rag in adjoining pockets. I took them out after a long errand and could not remember which bundle was supper.
  : My nose knew at once. I opened the cheese and discovered I'd wrapped the cloth inside like a very neat napkin.
  b : And the other pocket?
  : Empty apart from its own buckle. I'd spent a mile worrying about biting a perfectly decent piece of brass.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Name inside, clean wrapping out. | Fasten the fold with a dry iron pin.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One little gap between the lamp and the brim. | Keep the oily edge out of the starlight.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the hem above that soft patch. | Leave the mud to enjoy its own short journey.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A spare fold for the homeward caller. | Leave the hood over the wide chair tonight.

dlg resident.hub : Step over near my shoulder and my brim can shelter us both. A civil conversation takes very little shelter.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant self.workplace] : I help at #self.workplace#. Small wares, a tidy order and parcels that can be got safely home.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This much has come through without getting smudged. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : It's the spare corner again for you, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.bye : A sound seam between your business and the weather.

graft resident.hub
choice Does that hood really shelter two? -> second_nose
node second_nose
say A second nose quite comfortably. Add another pair of ears and we must walk very companionably. It makes a fine test of what a wolf means by a little help.
free
choice Isn't the outside ear left to get wet? -> outer_ear
choice The second fold looks very snug. -> hub
node outer_ear
say It depends who offers first. I take the wet one when I turn the brim. A real favour ought to cost the giver at least half a damp ear.
choice I'll remember whose ear paid. -> hub
choice I'll risk my own hood now. -> bye
